 """A binary classifier. eval.py calls fit(X, y) on the training split and predict(model, X) on new rows.
 
 X is a float array of shape (n, 16), y is 0/1 of shape (n,). numpy is the only dependency available.
+
+Logistic regression on a handful of engineered features. The shapes were found by fitting per-feature
+splines and a full quadratic model under 5-fold CV on the training split: the label depends on x0*x1,
+sin(2*x2), x3^2, x4^2, x5, |x6| and x7; the other inputs (including the high-variance x12..x15) add noise.
 """
 import numpy as np
 
 
